{"records":[{"id":"4mb5kjywkj","title":"Western Blot raw data of the manuscript titled \"In vivo CRISPR knockout screen identifies p47 as a suppressor for HER2+ breast cancer metastasis by regulating NEMO trafficking and autophagy flux\"","description":"The raw images of WB is for the reviewers' request when reviewing the manuscript titled \"In vivo CRISPR knockout screen identifies p47 as a suppressor for HER2+ breast cancer metastasis by regulating NEMO trafficking and autophagy flux\".","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-12-04T00:26:32.621Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/4mb5kjywkj","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/4mb5kjywkj"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Mingang","last_name":"Hao","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"vtvxykv2cr","title":"2020_Cell reports resubmission tables","description":"All tables associated with our paper titled \"High throughput CRISPR screening identifies genes involved in macrophage viability and inflammatory pathways\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-12-15T08:44:50.23Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/vtvxykv2cr","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/vtvxykv2cr"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Susan","last_name":"Carpenter","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Macrophage","Immunity","Innate Immunity","Screening","Pooled Analysis","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"sxrvzkr4hh","title":"Pooled in vitro and in vivo CRISPR-Cas9 screening identifies tumor suppressors in human colon organoids","description":"UMI validation screen, original data from in vivo tumor suppressor CRISPR/Cas9 screening experiment. Figure 6.\nExperimental setup: 281 tumor suppressor gRNAs, positive controls, neutral controls and gRNAs targeting essential genes were introduced into the CRISPR-UMI lentivirus (Michlits et al., 2017). Transduced AK organoids (APC-KO and KRASG12D) were transplanted subcutaneously in NSG mice followed by barcode sequencing of the tumor pool (from 10 mice) and 5 individual tumors. Clone and read number were determined by next generation sequencing. The conventional gRNA enrichment analysis was compared to UMI-CRISPR-screening with outlier removal.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-04-20T15:46:17.868Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/sxrvzkr4hh","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/sxrvzkr4hh"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Henner","last_name":"Farin","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cell Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"26r263sm6w","title":"Mosaic mutant analysis identifies PDGFRα/PDGFRβ as negative regulators of adipogenesis","description":"Quantitative data associated with the manuscript \"Mosaic mutant analysis identifies PDGFRα/PDGFRβ as negative regulators of adipogenesis\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-03-05T21:51:14.98Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/26r263sm6w","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/26r263sm6w"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Lorin","last_name":"Olson","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Hiromi","last_name":"Sakashita","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Adipose-Derived Mesenchymal Stem Cell"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"hvb39r62xw","title":"Massively parallel in vivo Perturb-seq reveals cell type-specific transcriptional networks in cortical development","description":"Raw and processed data associated with Zheng et al 2023 manuscript: the supplement tables, raw FASTQ files and processed Seurat objects are included. Code and pipeline repo at https://github.com/jinlabneurogenomics/aavperturbseq","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-09-07T16:45:41.475Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/hvb39r62xw","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/hvb39r62xw"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Xinhe","last_name":"Zheng","orcid":"0000-0002-4388-6724"},{"first_name":"Sean","last_name":"Simmons","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Kwanho","last_name":"Kim","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Joshua","last_name":"Levin","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Xin","last_name":"Jin","orcid":"0000-0003-2344-992X"}],"funders":[],"categories":["Genomics","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"tzhfpdymv9","title":"Massively parallel multicanonical simulations","description":"Generalized-ensemble Monte Carlo simulations such as the multicanonical method and similar techniques are among the most efficient approaches for simulations of systems undergoing discontinuous phase transitions or with rugged free-energy landscapes. As Markov chain methods, they are inherently serial computationally. It was demonstrated recently, however, that a combination of independent simulations that communicate weight updates at variable intervals allows for the efficient utilization of parallel computational resources for multicanonical simulations. Implementing this approach for the many-thread architecture provided by current generations of graphics processing units (GPUs), we show how it can be efficiently employed with of the order of 104 parallel walkers and beyond, thus constituting a versatile tool for Monte Carlo simulations in the era of massively parallel computing. We provide the fully documented source code for the approach applied to the paradigmatic example of the two-dimensional Ising model as starting point and reference for practitioners in the field.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2017-12-01T12:00:51.208Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/tzhfpdymv9","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/tzhfpdymv9"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jonathan","last_name":"Gross","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Johannes","last_name":"Zierenberg","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Martin","last_name":"Weigel","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Wolfhard","last_name":"Janke","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Computational Physics","Parallel Computing"],"journal_issn":["00104655"]},{"id":"65pfcj4j4m","title":"Protocol of CRISPR-Cas9 knockout screens for identifying ferroptosis regulators","description":"Ferroptosis, an iron-dependent programmed cell death triggered by excessive lipid peroxidation, has shown promising therapeutic potentials in human diseases. Here, we describe a protocol of a CRISPR-Cas9 loss-of-function screen to identify regulators in response to different inducers of ferroptosis. We emphasize the steps of library amplification, drug treatment, high-throughput sequencing preparation, and bioinformatics analysis using Model-based Analysis of Genome-wide CRISPR-Cas9 Knockout (MAGeCK). We also present a method to discover the regulators of ferroptosis and verify the potential targets efficiently.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-10-24T01:46:48.793Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/65pfcj4j4m","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/65pfcj4j4m"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Xin","last_name":"Yang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Wei","last_name":"Gu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["CRISPR/Cas9","Ferroptosis"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"bw5kfc5y6k","title":"Cardiomyocyte maturation on a cardiac mimetic matrix","description":"RNAseq of human induced pluripotent stem cell derived cardiomyocytes, cultured on control substrates, and our cardiomimetic matrix.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-03-22T16:36:50.023Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/bw5kfc5y6k","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/bw5kfc5y6k"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Yasir","last_name":"Suhail","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Kshitiz","last_name":"Kz","orcid":"0000-0003-4241-9427"},{"first_name":"Junaid","last_name":"Afzal","orcid":"0000-0002-2877-234X"}],"funders":[],"categories":["Induced Pluripotent Stem Cell","Cardiomyocyte"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"xvk2gk4hw3","title":"Data of Murine Trophoblast Organoids as a Model for Trophoblast Development and CRISPR/Cas9 Screening","description":"Raw data for figures in Murine Trophoblast Organoids as a Model for Trophoblast Development and CRISPR/Cas9 Screening","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-10-25T15:27:04.321Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/xvk2gk4hw3","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/xvk2gk4hw3"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Qian","last_name":"Mao","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Developmental Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"r5db9w567v","title":"Lipid Metabolism Remodeling in Human Cardiomyocyte Differentiation and Maturation","description":"In this study, the low-input trace lipidomics approach was utilized to analyze the dynamic changes of lipidomics during the differentiation process of human cardiomyocytes.Overall, our findings indicate that lipid species undergo a transition: from simple hydrocarbons with lower saturation in early embryonic stem cells to more complex lipids with longer hydrocarbon chains and higher unsaturation in later stages during CM differentiation. The simple lipid species in the early stage are suited for rapidly assembling basic membrane structures and serving as raw materials for synthesizing complex lipid molecules. In contrast, the complex lipid species in the later stage are crucial for maintaining membrane stability and fluidity during CM contraction; they can also act as second messengers to participate in more complex cellular signaling.\nFurthermore, the remodeling of the lipidome during this process partly reflects the metabolic transition from a glycolysis-dominated stem cell state to mature CMs reliant on oxidative phosphorylation. Current research remains in the basic stage. Future studies can build on the current findings regarding lipid unsaturation and specific lipid changes during cardiac differentiation to investigate related regulatory genes, further clarifying their regulatory mechanisms and deeper physiological roles. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-10-23T08:17:18.202Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/r5db9w567v","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/r5db9w567v"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Haite","last_name":"Tang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Raina","last_name":"Liu","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Zhiqiang","last_name":"Xiong","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Qiqi","last_name":"He","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Gang","last_name":"Lu","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Wai-Yee","last_name":"Chan","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Wuming","last_name":"Wang","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":null,"name":"Strategic Seed Funding for Collaborative Research Scheme from CUHK","grant_id":"#MK/WW/SSFCRS2324/8014/24jh"},{"id":null,"name":"Natural Science Foundation of China (NSFC)-Young Scientists Fund","grant_id":"#82200314"},{"id":null,"name":"Direct Grant for Research from CUHK","grant_id":"#2021.069 and #2022.082"},{"id":null,"name":"Innovation and Technology Commission of the Hong Kong Government grants ","grant_id":"GHX09721SZ and MHP00523"},{"id":null,"name":"the National Natural Science Foundation of China (NSFC)/Research Grants Council (RGC) Joint Research Scheme ","grant_id":"#N_CUHK428/22"},{"id":null,"name":"the Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK)–Shandong University (SDU) Joint Laboratory on Reproductive Genetics","grant_id":null}],"categories":["Cell Differentiation","Lipidomics","Cell Metabolism","Embryonic Stem Cell","Cardiomyocyte"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":135535,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":129,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":135535,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":134845,"restricted":67,"embargoed":623},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":2276},{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","count":1343},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":650},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Center","count":473},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":447},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":426},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"National Council for Scientific and Technological Development","count":409},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S. National Science Foundation","count":383},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","count":326},{"id":"https://ror.org/00hhkn466","name":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","count":269}],"source_stats":[{"id":"MENDELEY_DATA","name":"Mendeley Data","count":132903},{"id":"f881433a-b1cd-40d2-ab9f-4fd501f2d14b","name":"Elsevier Data Repository","count":1900},{"id":"a191461c-0227-403f-a1e9-621e0e0429cc","name":"San Raffaele Open Research Data Repository","count":185},{"id":"b07018a5-fee6-4df1-9d43-ff0d81ad75ed","name":"Bicocca Open Archive Research Data","count":136},{"id":"df228bbb-ac66-410f-8c66-f61608d63d95","name":"University of South Florida","count":77},{"id":"2a9d1b7d-e447-466f-888f-aa6f84e575e4","name":"Digital Commons Data@Becker","count":64},{"id":"72c28c45-627f-446b-8a48-af7c0a51a357","name":"Università Cattolica del Sacro C